1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,820
Three days in Seoul.

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:04,220
Palaces, markets

3
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:05,740
a city view at sunset

4
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:08,680
and one day that's completely yours.

5
00:00:09,066 --> 00:00:10,842
If this is your first time

6
00:00:10,842 --> 00:00:13,402
this plan keeps each day in one part of

7
00:00:13,402 --> 00:00:14,029
the city

8
00:00:14,029 --> 00:00:16,433
so you spend your time looking around

9
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:17,686
not changing trains.

10
00:00:17,686 --> 00:00:20,142
I'll show you the route for every day

11
00:00:20,142 --> 00:00:20,978
what to eat

12
00:00:20,978 --> 00:00:24,726
and the small mistakes that trip up first-time visitors.

13
00:00:25,236 --> 00:00:27,596
Let's start with a few things to sort out

14
00:00:27,596 --> 00:00:28,856
before day one.

15
00:00:29,646 --> 00:00:30,446
First

16
00:00:30,446 --> 00:00:32,646
check your dates.

17
00:00:32,646 --> 00:00:35,086
Gyeongbokgung Palace is closed on Tuesdays

18
00:00:35,086 --> 00:00:38,806
and Changdeokgung Palace is closed on Mondays.

19
00:00:38,806 --> 00:00:40,566
If your trip falls that way

20
00:00:40,566 --> 00:00:42,906
just swap day one and day three.

21
00:00:43,248 --> 00:00:44,308
Second

22
00:00:44,308 --> 00:00:46,768
get a transit card when you arrive.

23
00:00:46,768 --> 00:00:49,248
You tap it on the subway and on buses

24
00:00:49,248 --> 00:00:52,108
and transfers within a short time are discounted.

25
00:00:52,458 --> 00:00:52,906
Third

26
00:00:52,906 --> 00:00:54,923
install Naver Map or KakaoMap.

27
00:00:54,923 --> 00:00:57,724
Google Maps can show you places in Korea

28
00:00:57,724 --> 00:00:59,797
but its directions are limited

29
00:00:59,797 --> 00:01:02,318
so a Korean map app will save you a

30
00:01:02,318 --> 00:01:03,738
lot of guessing.

31
00:01:04,524 --> 00:01:06,564
Flying into Incheon?

32
00:01:06,564 --> 00:01:09,004
The AREX airport train is the simplest way

33
00:01:09,004 --> 00:01:10,564
into central Seoul

34
00:01:10,564 --> 00:01:12,964
and airport buses and taxis are good options

35
00:01:12,964 --> 00:01:16,364
if you have heavy bags or arrive late.

36
00:01:16,364 --> 00:01:18,824
Pick whichever drops you closest to your hotel.

37
00:01:19,230 --> 00:01:21,470
And where should you stay?

38
00:01:21,470 --> 00:01:24,670
Central Seoul works best for this plan.

39
00:01:24,670 --> 00:01:26,770
Around Gwanghwamun, Jongno

40
00:01:26,770 --> 00:01:28,870
City Hall or Myeongdong

41
00:01:28,870 --> 00:01:31,490
every stop is a short subway ride or a

42
00:01:31,490 --> 00:01:32,130
walk away.

43
00:01:32,496 --> 00:01:35,656
Day one is all about old Seoul

44
00:01:35,656 --> 00:01:37,836
and you can do the whole day on foot.

45
00:01:38,346 --> 00:01:41,306
Start early at Gyeongbokgung Palace

46
00:01:41,306 --> 00:01:44,006
the largest of Seoul's royal palaces from the

47
00:01:44,006 --> 00:01:45,586
Joseon dynasty.

48
00:01:45,586 --> 00:01:48,766
Get off at Gyeongbokgung Station on Line 3.

49
00:01:48,766 --> 00:01:50,666
If you arrive around opening time

50
00:01:50,666 --> 00:01:52,926
the big courtyards are much quieter.

51
00:01:53,964 --> 00:01:56,944
The changing of the royal guard at Gwanghwamun

52
00:01:56,944 --> 00:01:59,944
Gate usually happens at ten in the morning and

53
00:01:59,944 --> 00:02:01,664
two in the afternoon.

54
00:02:01,664 --> 00:02:03,084
And here's a fun one:

55
00:02:03,084 --> 00:02:04,644
if you wear hanbok

56
00:02:04,644 --> 00:02:06,404
the traditional dress

57
00:02:06,404 --> 00:02:08,924
entry to the palaces is free.

58
00:02:08,924 --> 00:02:11,184
There are rental shops near the station.

59
00:02:11,670 --> 00:02:14,850
Give the palace about two hours.

60
00:02:14,850 --> 00:02:18,270
Then walk east to Anguk and the hanok lanes

61
00:02:18,270 --> 00:02:19,810
of Bukchon.

62
00:02:19,810 --> 00:02:21,530
These are real homes

63
00:02:21,530 --> 00:02:25,550
so keep your voice down and stay out of doorways.

64
00:02:25,550 --> 00:02:27,730
Some parts of Bukchon now have visiting hours

65
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:28,990
for tourists

66
00:02:28,990 --> 00:02:30,910
so check the signs as you go.

67
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:34,760
When your feet need a rest

68
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:36,060
Anguk is full of cafes

69
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:38,960
and some are inside old hanok houses with

70
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:41,980
wooden beams and little courtyards.

71
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:42,580
Order at the counter

72
00:02:42,580 --> 00:02:45,720
and it's normal to sit as long as you like.

73
00:02:46,074 --> 00:02:47,154
In the afternoon

74
00:02:47,154 --> 00:02:49,469
head a few minutes south to Insadong.

75
00:02:49,469 --> 00:02:52,247
The main street and its side alleys are full

76
00:02:52,247 --> 00:02:53,584
of traditional crafts

77
00:02:53,584 --> 00:02:55,487
tea houses and small galleries.

78
00:02:55,487 --> 00:02:57,854
It's a good place for small souvenirs

79
00:02:57,854 --> 00:02:59,594
like hanji paper goods.

80
00:03:00,084 --> 00:03:03,163
If you want a quiet moment before dinner

81
00:03:03,163 --> 00:03:06,857
step into one of Insadong's traditional tea houses.

82
00:03:06,857 --> 00:03:09,813
Try a herbal tea like jujube or citron

83
00:03:09,813 --> 00:03:12,884
and enjoy a slower side of the city.

84
00:03:13,302 --> 00:03:17,102
Finish with an evening walk along Cheonggyecheon

85
00:03:17,102 --> 00:03:19,622
the stream that runs below street level from

86
00:03:19,622 --> 00:03:21,282
Cheonggye Plaza.

87
00:03:21,282 --> 00:03:22,822
It's lit up after dark

88
00:03:22,822 --> 00:03:23,822
it's free

89
00:03:23,822 --> 00:03:25,842
and it's an easy way to end a long

90
00:03:25,842 --> 00:03:26,722
first day.

91
00:03:27,072 --> 00:03:29,692
Day two is for food

92
00:03:29,692 --> 00:03:31,792
shopping and the best view of the city.

93
00:03:32,274 --> 00:03:33,910
Start at Gwangjang Market

94
00:03:33,910 --> 00:03:36,180
near Jongno 5-ga Station on Line 1.

95
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:39,137
It's one of Seoul's oldest markets and a great

96
00:03:39,137 --> 00:03:41,565
place for breakfast or an early lunch.

97
00:03:41,565 --> 00:03:42,885
Look for bindaetteok

98
00:03:42,885 --> 00:03:46,210
a crispy mung bean pancake fried right at the stall

99
00:03:46,210 --> 00:03:47,319
and mayak gimbap

100
00:03:47,319 --> 00:03:50,328
little rice rolls that are hard to stop eating.

101
00:03:50,328 --> 00:03:52,634
Bring some cash for the stalls.

102
00:03:53,124 --> 00:03:57,384
Then take the subway to Myeongdong on Line 4.

103
00:03:57,384 --> 00:04:00,804
It's packed with cosmetics shops and fashion stores

104
00:04:00,804 --> 00:04:04,544
and from late afternoon the street food stalls open.

105
00:04:04,544 --> 00:04:07,204
Many shops offer tax refunds for visitors

106
00:04:07,204 --> 00:04:09,464
so bring your passport when you go shopping.

107
00:04:10,686 --> 00:04:12,606
From late afternoon

108
00:04:12,606 --> 00:04:15,526
Myeongdong's main streets fill with food stalls.

109
00:04:15,526 --> 00:04:16,506
Grilled skewers

110
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:17,246
egg bread

111
00:04:17,246 --> 00:04:19,446
sweet pancakes called hotteok.

112
00:04:19,446 --> 00:04:21,286
Most stalls take cards now

113
00:04:21,286 --> 00:04:23,666
but keep a little cash just in case

114
00:04:23,666 --> 00:04:25,806
and look for the price on the sign before

115
00:04:25,806 --> 00:04:26,586
you order.

116
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,589
As the sun goes down

117
00:04:28,589 --> 00:04:30,825
go up Namsan to N Seoul Tower.

118
00:04:30,825 --> 00:04:34,121
From Myeongdong you can walk to the cable car

119
00:04:34,121 --> 00:04:36,357
or take a bus up the mountain.

120
00:04:36,357 --> 00:04:38,593
The view is best around sunset.

121
00:04:38,593 --> 00:04:41,594
Cable car and observatory times change with

122
00:04:41,594 --> 00:04:42,418
the season

123
00:04:42,418 --> 00:04:44,660
so check them that morning.

124
00:04:45,114 --> 00:04:48,034
Day three is yours.

125
00:04:48,034 --> 00:04:50,894
Each of these options fills about half a day

126
00:04:50,894 --> 00:04:51,974
so pick two.

127
00:04:52,332 --> 00:04:54,192
Want more history?

128
00:04:54,192 --> 00:04:57,392
Visit Changdeokgung Palace and its Secret Garden.

129
00:04:57,392 --> 00:04:59,132
The garden can only be seen on a guided

130
00:04:59,132 --> 00:05:00,772
tour with its own ticket

131
00:05:00,772 --> 00:05:02,032
and places are limited

132
00:05:02,032 --> 00:05:02,952
so book ahead.

133
00:05:03,342 --> 00:05:06,142
Into design and shopping?

134
00:05:06,142 --> 00:05:07,942
Go to Dongdaemun Design Plaza

135
00:05:07,942 --> 00:05:11,242
and the fashion malls around Dongdaemun that

136
00:05:11,242 --> 00:05:12,482
stay open late.

137
00:05:13,056 --> 00:05:15,876
Want to slow down like a local?

138
00:05:15,876 --> 00:05:17,976
Spend the afternoon in a Han River park

139
00:05:17,976 --> 00:05:19,696
like Yeouido.

140
00:05:19,696 --> 00:05:20,976
People picnic

141
00:05:20,976 --> 00:05:24,096
cycle and order fried chicken to the riverbank.

142
00:05:24,096 --> 00:05:25,476
Renting a bike is easy

143
00:05:25,476 --> 00:05:27,836
and there's always a convenience store nearby.

144
00:05:28,914 --> 00:05:31,514
Or relax properly at a jjimjilbang

145
00:05:31,514 --> 00:05:33,114
a Korean bathhouse.

146
00:05:33,114 --> 00:05:34,834
It's one of the most local things you can

147
00:05:34,834 --> 00:05:35,994
do in Seoul.

148
00:05:35,994 --> 00:05:38,274
Just read up on the etiquette before you go.

149
00:05:38,964 --> 00:05:42,164
And if you have more than three days

150
00:05:42,164 --> 00:05:44,144
explore neighbourhoods like Seongsu

151
00:05:44,144 --> 00:05:45,604
Hongdae or Itaewon

152
00:05:45,604 --> 00:05:47,984
or take a day trip out of the city

153
00:05:47,984 --> 00:05:50,024
like Suwon's Hwaseong Fortress

154
00:05:50,024 --> 00:05:51,684
an easy train ride away.

155
00:05:52,014 --> 00:05:55,834
Almost everything in this plan is on the subway.

156
00:05:55,834 --> 00:05:58,174
Tap your card in and out at the gates

157
00:05:58,174 --> 00:06:00,394
and use the same card on buses.

158
00:06:01,272 --> 00:06:04,872
Seoul's subway is easy for visitors.

159
00:06:04,872 --> 00:06:06,852
Lines have numbers and colours

160
00:06:06,852 --> 00:06:08,252
station names are in English

161
00:06:08,252 --> 00:06:10,472
and announcements are in English too.

162
00:06:10,472 --> 00:06:11,932
When you change lines

163
00:06:11,932 --> 00:06:14,272
just follow the colour of the line you want.

164
00:06:14,826 --> 00:06:18,518
Taxis are easy to find and fair for short trips.

165
00:06:18,518 --> 00:06:20,207
With the Kakao T app

166
00:06:20,207 --> 00:06:23,886
you can book one without speaking any Korean.

167
00:06:24,324 --> 00:06:25,332
Before you go

168
00:06:25,332 --> 00:06:28,412
here are four small mistakes that catch a lot

169
00:06:28,412 --> 00:06:30,224
of first-time visitors.

170
00:06:30,822 --> 00:06:31,176
One.

171
00:06:31,176 --> 00:06:32,709
Palaces on a weekend.

172
00:06:32,709 --> 00:06:36,600
Most sights are busiest on weekends and public holidays

173
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:39,724
so do the palaces on a weekday if you can.

174
00:06:39,724 --> 00:06:40,078
Two.

175
00:06:40,078 --> 00:06:41,788
Lunch after two o'clock.

176
00:06:41,788 --> 00:06:44,735
Many restaurants close for a break in the

177
00:06:44,735 --> 00:06:46,445
middle of the afternoon

178
00:06:46,445 --> 00:06:47,860
so eat lunch early.

179
00:06:47,860 --> 00:06:48,332
Three.

180
00:06:48,332 --> 00:06:49,982
No cash at the market.

181
00:06:49,982 --> 00:06:51,987
Cards work almost everywhere

182
00:06:51,987 --> 00:06:54,994
but carry a little cash for market stalls.

183
00:06:54,994 --> 00:06:55,701
And four.

184
00:06:55,701 --> 00:06:57,588
Trusting old opening hours.

185
00:06:57,588 --> 00:06:59,710
Hours and closing days change

186
00:06:59,710 --> 00:07:02,422
so check each place on a map app the

187
00:07:02,422 --> 00:07:03,842
morning you go.

188
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:06,800
And one bonus tip.

189
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:09,840
Convenience stores are your best friend in Seoul.

190
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:12,240
They're on almost every corner

191
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:14,160
many are open around the clock

192
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:15,820
and you can buy water

193
00:07:15,820 --> 00:07:17,080
snacks and a quick meal

194
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:19,300
and top up your transit card with cash.

195
00:07:19,746 --> 00:07:22,966
A few questions people often ask.

196
00:07:22,966 --> 00:07:25,186
Is three days enough for Seoul?

197
00:07:25,186 --> 00:07:27,306
It covers the main palaces

198
00:07:27,306 --> 00:07:28,786
a traditional market

199
00:07:28,786 --> 00:07:30,746
a shopping street and a city view

200
00:07:30,746 --> 00:07:32,546
at a comfortable pace.

201
00:07:32,844 --> 00:07:36,084
Which day should you visit Gyeongbokgung?

202
00:07:36,084 --> 00:07:38,104
Any day except Tuesday

203
00:07:38,104 --> 00:07:39,604
when it's closed.

204
00:07:39,604 --> 00:07:41,884
Weekday mornings are the quietest.

205
00:07:42,246 --> 00:07:44,906
Do you need to book anything?

206
00:07:44,906 --> 00:07:47,486
Most of this plan needs no booking at all.

207
00:07:47,486 --> 00:07:50,286
The one exception is the Secret Garden tour at

208
00:07:50,286 --> 00:07:51,246
Changdeokgung

209
00:07:51,246 --> 00:07:53,806
which has limited places.

210
00:07:53,806 --> 00:07:56,026
Popular restaurants can also have queues at

211
00:07:56,026 --> 00:07:56,946
busy times.

212
00:07:57,312 --> 00:08:00,552
So that's three days in Seoul.

213
00:08:00,552 --> 00:08:02,372
Day one, palaces

214
00:08:02,372 --> 00:08:04,512
hanok lanes and the stream.

215
00:08:04,512 --> 00:08:05,352
Day two

216
00:08:05,352 --> 00:08:06,932
a market breakfast

217
00:08:06,932 --> 00:08:09,632
Myeongdong and the sunset from Namsan.

218
00:08:09,632 --> 00:08:10,612
Day three

219
00:08:10,612 --> 00:08:11,872
whatever you love most.

220
00:08:12,210 --> 00:08:13,990
The full plan

221
00:08:13,990 --> 00:08:15,930
with links for every stop

222
00:08:15,930 --> 00:08:18,070
is on Korea Plainly.

223
00:08:18,070 --> 00:08:20,370
The link is in the description.

224
00:08:20,370 --> 00:08:22,090
If this helped

225
00:08:22,090 --> 00:08:23,550
subscribe for more plain

226
00:08:23,550 --> 00:08:25,130
practical guides to Korea.

227
00:08:25,130 --> 00:08:27,070
Have a wonderful trip to Seoul.

